  "reason": "Complete explicitly described 4D visible EFT after treating hidden supersymmetry breaking as external spurion; unified origins are not appended as extra factors.",
  "inspected_scope": "P24 Section2/2.3 visible GEM EFT, plus Section3.2.1 bachelor inventory, PDFp11",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "p24-fields",
      "locator": "P24 Section2 PDFp4/printedp3, Figure1 and model-definition paragraph; source supersoft components Eqs.(2.5)-(2.6) PDFp5",
      "fact": "MSSM N=1 matter and both Hu,Hd retained; add one adjoint chiral Aj for each Gi=SU3,SU2,U1. Each Aj contains complex scalar and independent LH Weyl, with exact weights SU3 adjoint[1,1],SU2 adjoint[2],U1 adjoint singlet. Therefore complex neutral real-type Aj scalar gives two real-module copies; fermion gives one Weyl. MSSM adjoint gaugino already counted, so Dirac gauginos are not additional fermions on top of both Weyl constituents.",
      "basis": "fresh_source_statement_and_superfield_expansion"
    },
    {
      "id": "p24-spurion",
      "locator": "P24 Section2.3 PDFp6/printedp5, first paragraphs",
      "fact": "Source explicitly defines renormalizable effective theory with soft breaking and external W'alpha/M=theta_alpha mD spurion. Accepted visible EFT has dynamical gSM only; background hidden U1 connection/unknown hidden matter is not appended as an incompletely specified gauge factor. No bulk/brane or unified regime is summed into this 4D EFT.",
      "basis": "source_explicit_spurion_EFT_scope"
    },
    {
      "id": "p24-bachelors",
      "locator": "P24 Section3.2.1 PDFp11/printedp10, paragraph beginning ESP and bachelor fields",
      "fact": "One chiral vectorlike doublet pair (1,2,+/-1/2), two chiral charged-singlet pairs (1,1,+/-1), and four chiral neutral singlets (1,1,0), beyond MSSM+Aj. Each neutral complex scalar gives two real-module copies; no arbitrary extra singlets added.",
      "basis": "fresh_explicit_bachelor_inventory"
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Visible gSM EFT only, with hidden W'alpha/M external spurion. Supersymmetry-breaking hidden/UV completion and GUT-breaking Higgs sector are not part of, or claimed by, this regime. Existing historical hidden-sector/alternate-regime assertions remain provenance."
